From a4416155c419b0f1e95af1e6c23244db217f3b72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:32:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kms-worker): Profile Q5 reads the state at B_Q
 (lifecycle Phase 5)

Two cases of the delegation cutoff now read the host chain's state at
the activation block B_Q:

- adopted code: a delegator whose code is regular now but was empty
  or an EIP-7702/7851 indicator at B_Q adopted it after B_Q (EIP-8298
  SETCODEFROM), which reading today's code cannot tell from a
  contract's; the cutoff applies to every change since B_Q;
- successions: for a retired account the registry's delegated view
  answers true only for its confirmed successor, which a key still
  accepted after B_Q could have designated and confirmed; the
  succession counts only if the same successor was confirmed at B_Q.

Unreadable state at B_Q fails closed. Unit tests for both decisions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
