 //!   before `B_Q`. The registry has no getter for that block, so it is read from the ACL's ERC-7201 storage
 //!   (`UserDecryptionDelegation.lastBlockDelegateOrRevoke`) with `eth_getStorageAt`, only for an ACL version whose
